  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 1153 PM CDT Sat Oct 31 2026\n\nMonday through Wednesday\nAssessment...high (>80%) confidence on a storm system bringing\nsome rain to the area along with warmer than normal temperatures.\n\nAlthough there are differences between the global models, they have \nbeen consistent in taking the center of the significant system well \nto the west of the area. The net result will be much warmer than \nnormal temperatures for the area along with windy conditions. \nPeriodic rounds of rain will be seen with the best chances being \nMonday night into Tuesday.\n\nThe overall timing for the best chances for rain also agrees with \nthe surge of moisture from the Pacific along with some from the \nGulf. The model PWATs with the moisture surge are 1.5+ inches which \nwould exceed the local sounding climatology. Such moisture also \nyields a high probability of locally heavy rainfall, especially with \nany thunderstorms.\n\nThunderstorms will be possible since we'll be in the warm sector of \nthe storm. The signal for strong to severe storms is mixed but \nvarious ML runs suggests a severe potential in the Plains. Back in \neastern Iowa the signal is being lost in the overall background \nnoise.\n\nOnce the main cold front and a secondary low sweep through the area \non Wednesday, spotty showers and sprinkles will be possible the \nsecond half of the work week.\n\nTemperatures through the entire week will average above normal for \nearly November.",
